  "summary": "Claire Lomas, a charity campaigner who was paralyzed in a riding accident in 2007 and raised nearly £1 million through athletic events, has died at the age of 44 following an accident in Jordan. Lomas, who lived in Melton, Leicestershire, gained fame for completing the 2012 London Marathon in a bionic suit and lighting the Paralympic cauldron. Her family has requested privacy as they grieve. Lomas sustained her injuries during the Osberton Horse Trials in 2007. She also completed the Great North Run while pregnant in 2016, again using her bionic suit."
